/T (Forget complicated programs and gym jargon. Real fitness rests on three pillars working together: strength, cardio, and mobility & recovery. None of them is the "right" one. They each do a job, and they do it best as a team.)
/E (Forget complicated programs and gym jargon. Real fitness rests on three pillars working together: strength, cardio, and mobility & recovery. None of them is the "right" one. They each do a job, and they do it best as a team.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
438 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 214 0 R
/T (Strength builds and shapes you, and protects your joints for life. Cardio looks after your heart, your stamina, and your mood. Mobility and recovery are where the results actually lock in. When you stop chasing one and start treating all three as teammates, movement gets a lot quieter and a lot kinder.)
